# CSS consolidation rules

## Architecture

- Authored CSS lives only under root `css/`.
- Shared styles load through `css/main.css`.
- Assignment CSS → `css/assignments/`; Team Teaching CSS → `css/team-teaching/`.
- Keep cascade layers: `tokens → base → layout → components → utilities`.
- Reuse shared tokens, shell/layout, nav, cards, buttons, and forms; do not duplicate them.
- Keep topic-specific styles on their own pages/sheets only.

## New Team Teaching demos

- Put HTML in the matching unit directory; CSS in `css/team-teaching/`.
- Load `css/main.css` + the demo sheet; use `.page-shell`, shared nav, theme menu, and `js/theme-preference.js`.
- Support light / dark / system via semantic color tokens (no hardcoded theme colors).
- Use trailing-slash directory links.
- Add finished demos to homepage Team Teaching + README only when asked.

## Workflow

- Do only the requested task; no unrelated refactors.
- Preserve assignment requirements and behavior.
- Prefer simple, readable CSS/HTML.
- Before finishing implementation work: verify affected pages and run `pnpm build`.
- Report changes, test results, and remaining issues.
- Do not stage, commit, merge, push, reset, or switch branches without explicit permission.
